# GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 — msgpack OOB-read. This is pip's VENDORED copy
# (site-packages/pip/_vendor/msgpack), not an app dependency. pip is build-time
# tooling only; the running app never calls pip, so it's not in the attack surface.
# No fix available: current pip (26.2.1) still bundles msgpack 1.1.2.
# Revisit when pip vendors msgpack >= 1.2.1. Added 2026-09-27.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964

# CVE-2025-47273 — setuptools PackageIndex path traversal. The INSTALLED setuptools
# is 84.0.0 (patched, verified in the build log). Trivy flags a phantom 70.3.0
# reference bundled inside pip's build tooling (PkgPath: none) — not an importable
# or runtime package, and only relevant when using setuptools to INSTALL packages,
# which the running app never does. Added 2026-09-27.
CVE-2025-47273

# CVE-2026-97687 / CVE-2026-97689 — urllib3 TLS-interception + DoS. The INSTALLED
# urllib3 (used by botocore at runtime) is 2.8.0 (patched). Trivy flags pip's
# VENDORED copy at site-packages/pip/_vendor/urllib3 (_version.py pins 2.7.0) — pip
# is build-time tooling, never imported by the running app. No runtime exposure.
# Remove once the backend moves to a multi-stage/distroless image (no pip shipped).
# Added 2026-10-01.
CVE-2026-97687
CVE-2026-97689
